Do not use Mozilla's update server

Hallow builds the update framework for its update UI, but must never ask
Mozilla's update server (aus5.mozilla.org) for updates. Without an [AppUpdate]
URL, Firefox's MAR update service has nothing to check; Linux packages update
through LinuxPackageUpdater (see patches/0007).

diff --git a/build/application.ini.in b/build/application.ini.in
index 6df13230a4..9cf90458d4 100644
--- a/build/application.ini.in
+++ b/build/application.ini.in
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ ServerURL=@MOZ_CRASHREPORTER_URL@/submit?id=@MOZ_APP_ID@&version=@MOZ_APP_VERSIO
 #endif
 
 #if MOZ_UPDATER
-[AppUpdate]
-URL=https://@MOZ_APPUPDATE_HOST@/update/6/%PRODUCT%/%VERSION%/%BUILD_ID%/%BUILD_TARGET%/%LOCALE%/%CHANNEL%/%OS_VERSION%/%SYSTEM_CAPABILITIES%/%DISTRIBUTION%/%DISTRIBUTION_VERSION%/update.xml
+; Hallow has no Firefox-style (MAR) update server, so there is no [AppUpdate]
+; URL and Mozilla's update server is never contacted. Linux packages update
+; through the system package manager instead (LinuxPackageUpdater.sys.mjs).
 #endif
